# api/openapi.json is machine-generated (api/src/generate-openapi.ts writes LF
# unconditionally) and is diffed by the pre-push hook (.husky/pre-push) to
# detect drift from the real API. Without this, Windows' core.autocrlf=true
# (the default here, confirmed 2026-09-07, no .gitattributes existed before
# this) normalizes it to CRLF on checkout, so every regeneration shows as a
# full-file diff from line endings alone -- not from real content changes --
# which would make the hook block every push. Pinning eol=lf keeps the
# checked-out file byte-identical to what the generator writes.
api/openapi.json text eol=lf
